## **Performance Implications & Optimization Strategies**

**Bottlenecks:**
- Multiple high-res textures = GPU memory pressure
- Inefficient buffer updates (per-frame upload)
- Large framebuffers = more bandwidth
- Overdraw from blending/mask
- Instancing = draw call reduction, but per-instance data can be heavy

**Strategies:**
- Use compressed textures where possible (e.g., .ktx, .dds)
- Minimize per-frame buffer updates; use STATIC/DYNAMIC hints
- Use scissor and viewport to restrict rendering to visible area
- Prefer instancing for similar objects
- Batch draw calls (sort by material/texture)

